{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they went three days.</b> When Israel went out from Egypt they took sweet waters in their vessels. When the waters ran out, they immediately complained, as it is said: ״וילונו העם״. They should have immediately asked for water, but instead they immediately complained. Another interpretation: ״וילכו שלשת ימים״ — darshanim of remez said: three days they walked in the wilderness and found no Torah, which is likened to water, and therefore they rebelled; and therefore the early ones enacted reading from the Torah on Sheni and Chamishi, so that three days should not pass without Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The Hebrew appears to contain a shortened/elliptic phrase: 'כלו המים נתרעמו' rendered as 'when the waters ran out, they complained,' though the syntax is compressed and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:18.429205685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}